---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro'
import Capture from '../components/Capture.astro'
import SurfaceLab from '../components/SurfaceLab.astro'
import { connectors, doc, packages, releases, repo, shot, subscriptions } from '../lib/content'
---

<Page>
  <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">A desktop workspace for the pi coding agent</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Parallel coding. <br />Without losing <br /><span>the thread.</span></h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-summary">
      <p class="hero-lede">
        Several tasks. Separate branches. The code, the agent’s changes, and the result in one
        place.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bring your models and subscriptions. Add pi extensions for the tools your work needs.
        Phosphor makes it all visible.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="action action-primary" href="/guides/"
          >Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
        <a class="action action-text" href="#work"
          >See the workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="hero-meta mono">
        <span>macOS / Linux / Windows</span><span>Open source · MIT</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-proof">
      <Capture
        image={shot('home')}
        alt="Phosphor’s lane dashboard with parallel sessions, a ready-to-merge task, and project usage."
        caption="See which task needs you next"
        sizes="(max-width: 480px) 92vw, (max-width: 1422px) 90vw, 1280px"
        eager
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / Keep the work legible</p><h2>
            Start with<br />a conversation.
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Describe the task in a familiar chat workspace. Follow the agent’s steps, inspect its
          edits, and keep each conversation on its own branch.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Capture
        class="workflow-chat"
        image={shot('chat')}
        alt="Phosphor’s chat-focused layout with a session sidebar, conversation, inline edit, and composer, with no auxiliary pane open."
        caption="The conversation first, with the agent’s work in reach"
      />
      <div class="numbered-notes">
        <article>
          <span>01 / ISOLATE</span><h3>Give a task its own branch.</h3><p>
            Open a folder, choose a model, and start in a Git worktree. Another task can work in a
            separate checkout.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article id="transcript">
          <span>02 / INSPECT</span><h3>Read the work as it runs.</h3><p>
            Open tool arguments and output. Inspect an edit’s diff. Review changed files against the
            session baseline, or revert a file.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article id="artifacts">
          <span>03 / KEEP</span><h3>Keep more than the answer.</h3><p>
            Plans, diagrams, and interactive pages become versioned artifacts. Reopen the session to
            read, revise, or compare them.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="source-line">
        <a class="text-link" href="/guides/#first-task">Try your first task →</a><a
          class="text-link"
          href={doc('lanes.md')}>Lanes and PR status ↗</a
        ><a class="text-link" href={doc('extensions.md#the-artifact-tools-and-what-each-one-costs')}
          >Artifact behavior ↗</a
        >
      </div>
      <SurfaceLab />
      <details class="disclosure">
        <summary>Inspect changes and keep the result <span>+</span></summary><div
          class="capture-pair"
        >
          <Capture
            image={shot('changes')}
            alt="An inline edit with the Changes pane beside the conversation."
            caption="Inspect the agent’s edits"
          />
          <Capture
            image={shot('artifacts')}
            alt="A document in the versioned artifact pane beside its conversation."
            caption="The result has a place of its own"
          />
        </div><p class="fineprint">
          PR status is read through gh. The guided merge is local, not a GitHub merge. Artifact HTML
          is isolated with no network; the agent’s tools are not sandboxed by that isolation.
        </p>
      </details>
      <p class="fineprint" id="sessions">
        Pick up saved sessions, fork a conversation, or queue a follow-up while the agent works. For
        repeatable tasks, <a class="text-link" href={doc('routines.md')}>local routines</a> create fresh
        sessions on a schedule while your computer is awake. They are not cloud jobs or a cross-session
        orchestrator.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="models" class="section alternate">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / Use what you already have</p><h2>
            Your models.<br />Your subscriptions.
          </h2>
        </div><p class="section-intro">
          Use a supported account login, an API key, or a custom endpoint. Switch models mid-session
          and keep the conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="subscription-grid">
        {
          subscriptions.map(({ name, plan, route }) => (
            <article>
              <>
                <h3>{name}</h3>
                <p class="mono">{plan}</p>
                <p>{route}</p>
              </>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="split feature-detail">
        <div class="copy-column">
          <h3 class="subheading">Know which account<br />is doing the work.</h3><p>
            Keep multiple Claude logins. Choose one for new sessions, use them in order, or
            distribute new sessions round robin. Each running session keeps its assigned account.
          </p><p>
            Open the context meter for reported token and cost counts, estimated composition, and
            available Claude plan usage. Provider limits still apply.
          </p><a class="action action-text" href="/guides/claude-code/"
            >Set up Claude and multiple accounts →</a
          ><a class="text-link" href={doc('chat.md#what-the-context-meters-popover-shows')}
            >Understand the context meter ↗</a
          >
        </div>
        <Capture
          image={shot('models')}
          alt="Searchable models grouped by provider in Phosphor’s composer."
          caption="Choose the model for your next turn"
        />
      </div>
      <p class="fineprint">
        Claude subscription access needs the Claude Code CLI and the pi-claude-cli package. ChatGPT
        uses pi’s native Codex OAuth. Subscriptions and API usage are billed by their providers, not
        Phosphor. <a class="text-link" href="/guides/#sign-in">Choose your sign-in route →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="extensions" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / The extensions make it yours</p><h2>
            Start with coding.<br />Add your capabilities.
          </h2>
        </div><p class="section-intro">
          pi supplies the agent loop. Packages add the tools: web research, connected services,
          delegation, and more. Phosphor gives them a workspace and settings you can inspect.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="package-grid">
        {
          packages.map(({ name, benefit, id }) => (
            <a class="package-card" href={`/guides/extensions/#${id}`}>
              <>
                <span class="mono">OPTIONAL PI PACKAGE</span>
                <h3>
                  {name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                </h3>
                <p>{benefit}</p>
              </>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="source-line">
        <a class="action action-primary" href="/guides/extensions/">Build your extension setup →</a
        ><a class="text-link" href="https://pi.dev/packages">Explore pi packages ↗</a>
      </div>
      <aside class="boundary-note">
        <strong>Included versus installed</strong><p>
          Artifacts, context breakdown, and Phosphor’s other bundled extensions are included. The
          packages above are optional installs in Settings → Extensions. Start a new session after
          installation. Packages execute code with your permissions, so review what you install.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="connectors" class="section alternate">
    <div class="container">
      <span id="gateways"></span>
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">04 / Bring your services into the task</p><h2>
            Your tools.<br />In the same session.
          </h2>
        </div><p class="section-intro">
          Add the MCP adapter, then connect the services you want the agent to use. No separate
          chat, no pasted context every time.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="connector-grid">
        {
          connectors.map(({ name, use, id }) => (
            <a href={`/guides/connectors/#${id}`}>
              <>
                <h3>
                  {name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
                </h3>
                <p>{use}</p>
              </>
            </a>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <Capture
        image={shot('guide-connectors')}
        alt="MCP Connectors settings with a connected-server list and the catalog of available services, using example configuration."
        caption="Add, sign in, test, or reconnect from Settings"
        provenance="Settings demo · example data"
      />
      <div class="source-line">
        <a class="action action-primary" href="/guides/connectors/">Connect your first service →</a
        ><a class="text-link" href="/guides/connectors/#custom">Add a custom MCP server →</a>
      </div>
      <p class="fineprint">
        Connector setup and Test run without a model call. Using tools during a task can consume
        model tokens and service quota. The adapter owns OAuth credentials. Slack requires your own
        registered app; access to every service depends on its permissions and your account.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="install" class="section install-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Start here</p><h2>One folder.<br />One useful task.</h2></div><div
          class="copy-column"
        >
          <p class="section-intro">
            Install pi and Phosphor, sign in to a provider, then add the extensions your work needs.
            The guides walk through the actual settings.
          </p><a class="action action-primary" href="/guides/">Installation and first task →</a><a
            class="text-link"
            href={`${releases}/latest`}>Download release assets ↗</a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-grid">
        <a href="/guides/claude-code/"
          ><h3>Claude Code + accounts ↗</h3><p>
            Install the provider, sign in, test it, and route new sessions.
          </p></a
        ><a href="/guides/extensions/"
          ><h3>Choose your extensions ↗</h3><p>
            What is included, what to install, and how packages apply.
          </p></a
        ><a href="/guides/connectors/"
          ><h3>Connect your services ↗</h3><p>
            MCP setup, permissions, sign-in, testing, and custom servers.
          </p></a
        >
      </div>
      <p class="fineprint">
        MIT licensed. Runs on your computer, not a hosted coding service. Tools have full
        permissions by default; providers and services receive what you send them. <a
          class="text-link"
          href="/guides/#trust">Understand the trust boundary →</a
        >
      </p>
      <div class="source-line" id="feature-index">
        <a class="text-link" href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/README.md`}>Technical documentation ↗</a
        ><a class="text-link" href={`${repo}/issues`}>Get help or report a problem ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
